          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What will happen if I take excess amount of any of the minerals or vitamins?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.404,
            0.083,
            0.882,
            0.139
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "which are caused by a lack of specific nutrients in the diet. These are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "deficiency diseases",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and are also non-communicable."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.142,
            0.883,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Diseases such as cancer, diabetes, and asthma may often persist for a long time (more than 3 months) and are referred to as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "chronic diseases",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.201,
            0.883,
            0.31
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Diabetes is a common disease which is becoming more prevalent in adults as well as children. In fact, India now has one of the highest numbers of people with diabetes in the world. It often develops due to a combination of hormonal imbalances, unhealthy eating habits, lack of physical activity, being overweight or obese, and other reasons."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.31,
            0.882,
            0.349
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us learn more about the causes of non-communicable diseases and their prevention."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.269,
            0.368,
            0.611,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 3.5: Let us survey"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.406,
            0.882,
            0.444
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Find out the three most common lifestyle-related diseases in your neighbourhood"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.447,
            0.883,
            0.503
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Talk to a doctor, nurse, health worker or even a family member who knows about health and what kind of lifestyle changes can help prevent or manage these diseases."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.507,
            0.882,
            0.543
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You can also consult trusted health websites, books, teachers and doctors."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
